  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "Number of alkanes obtained on electrolysis of a mixture of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COONa</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>COONa</mi></math> is_____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>An aqueous solution of sodium or potassium salt of carboxylic acid is electrolysed in this reaction, resulting in the dissociation of the salt into a carboxylate ion and sodium or potassium ions. </p><p>The total number of different alkanes are formed when the following mixture is subjected to electrolysis:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>COONa</mi><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></msub><mo> </mo><mi>and</mi><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><msub><mi>COONa</mi><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></msub></math> </p><p>In this ethane, butane and propane are formed.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COONa</mi><mo>→</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>∙</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>COONa</mi><mo>→</mo><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>∙</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>∙</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>∙</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>∙</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>∙</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>So, the total number of alkanes formed here will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></p>",
